Package: NADIA
Type: Package
Title: Missing Value-Aware Differential Abundance Analysis of DIA Proteomics Data
Version: 0.99.1
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Sergio",
    family = "Ciordia",
    email = "sciordia@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5726-853X"))
Description: Provides an end-to-end workflow for differential abundance
    analysis of protein quantification data, with particular attention to
    missing values in data-independent acquisition (DIA) proteomics.
    Quantification reports exported from Spectronaut, DIA-NN and Proteome
    Discoverer for TMT and label-free experiments (DDA/DIA) are converted into
    a common data structure, normalised, optionally batch-corrected, imputed and
    analysed using limma or limpa. The package includes individual and two-stage
    imputation strategies that treat values assumed to be missing at random and
    missing not at random separately. Data-driven functions evaluate and rank
    normalisation and imputation workflows using simulated missingness or
    spike-in datasets with known ground truth, allowing method selection to be
    justified for each dataset. Results can be explored through interactive
    Highcharts visualisations, static ggplot2 and ComplexHeatmap figures, and
    sortable tables.
